WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.890
Could Marvel be planning even more shocking
deaths in their "Spider-Man" franchise?

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:06.859
Keep watching to find out why they might be!

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:12.220
Cap had such a beautiful ending in "Avengers:
Endgame" with Peggy Carter, and if that was

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:16.129
tarnished in any way, fans might take to the
streets.

00:00:16.129 --> 00:00:20.380
Leading up to "Avengers: Endgame," fans long
suspected that either Tony or Steve would

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.369
die, with many assuming there wasn't a world
where both would meet their end.

00:00:24.369 --> 00:00:29.510
All across social media, MCU stans guessed
who would perish out of the two, and it seemed

00:00:29.510 --> 00:00:31.449
to be split right down the middle.

00:00:31.449 --> 00:00:35.890
In a popular Reddit thread, MCU fans were
forced to choose between the two men, but

00:00:35.890 --> 00:00:39.520
there was no consensus among the dozens of
users who participated.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:44.690
It's simple; no one wanted either man to die,
but for the story's sake, one had to.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:49.540
With Tony's death set in stone in the Sacred
Timeline, losing Steve as well in the future

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:54.690
would just be too much — and bringing him
back only to kill him off would be even worse.

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:58.800
Just ask "Star Wars" fans!

00:00:58.800 --> 00:00:59.940
“RAHHHHH!”

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:01.090
"NO!"

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:06.499
One thing is absolutely certain: if they kill
Thor, we riot!

00:01:06.499 --> 00:01:11.189
With both Natasha and Tony six feet under,
and Steve off living in some other timeline,

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:15.310
the only remaining original Avengers we have
left are Thor, Hawkeye, and the Hulk.

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.859
Of those, Thor is easily the most popular,
so if he were to die, it would be nothing

00:01:19.859 --> 00:01:21.890
but a big bummer.

00:01:21.890 --> 00:01:25.670
It would have to be someone or something serious
to take him out, of course.

00:01:25.670 --> 00:01:30.350
But while that might make for a great scene,
we'd really rather avoid it altogether.

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:34.310
There's no telling what fate awaits him in
"Thor: Love and Thunder," but we do know that

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:37.789
Hemsworth wants to play the character forever,
telling This Morning in 2019,

00:01:37.789 --> 00:01:41.189
"I'd play this character for as long as anyone
let me, you know.

00:01:41.189 --> 00:01:43.969
As I've said, I've loved it so much."

00:01:44.969 --> 00:01:48.829
If we were to list some of the most badass
people in all of the MCU, you better believe

00:01:48.829 --> 00:01:51.759
Okoye is going to be near the top of that
list.

00:01:51.759 --> 00:01:56.290
With no superpowers, the Wakandan has proven
she's a force to be reckoned with, knocking

00:01:56.290 --> 00:02:00.709
out her fair share of Outriders in both the
Battle of Wakanda and the Battle of Earth.

00:02:00.709 --> 00:02:06.029
She is fiercely loyal to her home country,
even putting it above her love for her partner

00:02:06.029 --> 00:02:07.229
in "Black Panther."

00:02:07.229 --> 00:02:11.909
Okoye's dedication to her people and whatever
mission is at hand makes her easy to root

00:02:11.909 --> 00:02:13.659
for, no matter what film she's in.

00:02:13.659 --> 00:02:17.849
We know she'll be appearing in "Black Panther:
Wakanda Forever" and the untitled Wakanda

00:02:17.849 --> 00:02:22.060
Disney+ series, and we hope she makes it out
of the latter alive.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:26.659
We hope T'Challa's family and closest allies
make it through each and every impending battle

00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:29.270
so they can continue to honor his legacy.

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:35.129
This one should go without saying, but the
death of Happy Hogan would absolutely crush

00:02:35.129 --> 00:02:36.510
fans of the MCU.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.260
He has been in the universe since day one,
appearing in six films as one of Tony Stark's

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:44.349
best friends, and as a mentor to Peter Parker.

00:02:44.349 --> 00:02:48.739
Happy just has that good guy quality about
him, and watching him almost die in "Iron

00:02:48.739 --> 00:02:52.569
Man 3" had us wanting revenge on Aldrich Killian
ourselves.

00:02:52.569 --> 00:02:56.569
It turns out Happy was supposed to die in
the film, according to storyboards from the

00:02:56.569 --> 00:02:57.569
first script.

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:02.219
We're not sure why the change was made, opting
to have Happy survive the explosion, but we're

00:03:02.219 --> 00:03:05.450
sure glad they decided to go with a more positive
outcome.

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:09.969
How the character is changed by the events
of "Spider-Man: No Way Home" remains to be

00:03:09.969 --> 00:03:13.689
seen, but here's hoping he finally gets a
true Happy ending.

00:03:14.689 --> 00:03:18.400
Rocket might be a little bit of a jerk most
of the time, but we know it's because he's

00:03:18.400 --> 00:03:20.629
suffered from quite a difficult life.

00:03:20.629 --> 00:03:24.379
He definitely has strong feelings when it
comes to those he loves, primarily for Groot

00:03:24.379 --> 00:03:28.110
as we saw him weep when his friend first died
in "Guardians of the Galaxy."

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:33.730
Um, and then again when Groot died the second
time in "Avengers: Infinity War."

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:38.650
If Rocket were to die in an upcoming project,
we suspect audiences wouldn't take it very

00:03:38.650 --> 00:03:39.650
well.

00:03:39.650 --> 00:03:43.739
To be fair, whenever an animal dies in a movie,
it always seems to have a more significant

00:03:43.739 --> 00:03:45.980
impact on the viewer than when a human dies.

00:03:45.980 --> 00:03:48.849
But we don't need any "Old Yeller" moments
in the MCU.

00:03:48.849 --> 00:03:54.360
Seeing a poor little raccoon — albeit a
wisecracking, mutated one — die on the big

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:57.170
screen would be truly devastating.

00:03:57.170 --> 00:04:00.069
Just take Peter Quill instead, we're begging
you!

00:04:01.069 --> 00:04:06.870
Florence Pugh took the MCU by storm after
debuting as Yelena Belova in "Black Widow."

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.420
Serving as the sister of Natasha Romanoff,
the former assassin helped fight back against

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.909
the baddies to take down the Red Room, ultimately
coming out victorious.

00:04:13.909 --> 00:04:18.370
The film wasn't without its flaws, but it
was widely accepted that one of the best things

00:04:18.370 --> 00:04:22.340
about "Black Widow" was Yelena, thanks to
Pugh's stellar portrayal.

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:26.680
From the way she poked fun at her sister's
superhero landing to her convincing breakdown

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.139
at the family reunion, Yelena is one of the
more relatable MCU characters out there, and

00:04:31.139 --> 00:04:35.270
fans only grew to love her hore thanks to
her surprise appearance in the Disney+ series

00:04:35.270 --> 00:04:37.240
"Hawkeye," which tied everything together.

00:04:37.240 --> 00:04:41.940
"You got so much time with her."

00:04:41.940 --> 00:04:43.410
"Yes, I did."

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:47.740
Someone needs to carry on Natasha's legacy,
and there is no one better to do it than her.

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:52.850
If Marvel kills off Yelena somewhere down
the line, it's going to be one hell of a hit

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.100
to the MCU fandom.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.030
Spider-Man has always been one of the most
widely loved superheroes, and the massive

00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:03.860
success of the Sam Raimi -directed trilogy
in the early-mid '00s is definitely proof

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:07.810
of how much fans always wanted to see the
web-slinger on the big screen.

00:05:07.810 --> 00:05:11.710
Star Tom Holland does a stellar job of portraying
the MCU's Spidey.

00:05:11.710 --> 00:05:15.840
He brings an innocence to the character in
ways not captured by Tobey Maguire or Andrew

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.360
Garfield, and his naive nature fits the teenage
hero to a tee.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:24.830
Technically, yes, we did see Peter die in
the finale of "Avengers: Infinity War," and

00:05:24.830 --> 00:05:28.500
it was the biggest gut punch of them all.

00:05:28.500 --> 00:05:32.380
Despite Holland being in the MCU a shorter
amount of time compared to other fan-favorites,

00:05:32.380 --> 00:05:37.569
his "Infinity War" death proved how much audiences
have accepted his version of Spider-Man.

00:05:37.569 --> 00:05:44.120
Putting the permanent kibosh on Tom Holland's
Peter would leave the MCU fandom reeling for sure.

00:05:44.797 --> 00:05:50.470
Groot made his MCU debut in "Guardians of
the Galaxy," and was immediately loved by

00:05:50.470 --> 00:05:55.890
all, despite only speaking four different
words in the entire film — five if you count

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:56.890
his name.

00:05:56.890 --> 00:06:01.900
Groot is fiercely loyal, especially to Rocket,
and he has a ride-or-die nature that isn't

00:06:01.900 --> 00:06:04.200
evident in all Marvel film characters.

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.620
This was evident in his ultimate sacrifice
at the end of the movie, where he creates

00:06:07.620 --> 00:06:11.590
a cradle out of his body to save the rest
of the Guardians from an otherwise deadly

00:06:11.590 --> 00:06:12.600
crash.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:17.840
Viewers fell for the talking tree in just
two hours, and his death in the film was shocking.

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:22.639
We had just been introduced to this new superhero
team, and losing one of the members right

00:06:22.639 --> 00:06:25.280
off the bat was a bold writing choice.

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:29.010
Luckily, we didn't have to wallow in our grief
for too long as it was revealed in the movie's

00:06:29.010 --> 00:06:33.230
finale that a part of his shattered body was
planted, and a new Groot was born.

00:06:33.230 --> 00:06:39.129
While teenage Groot tends to be annoyingly
angsty, we know that inside he's pure of heart.

00:06:39.129 --> 00:06:43.910
Watching Groot suffer a permanent death would
be pretty difficult, and watching other Guardians

00:06:43.910 --> 00:06:48.100
go before bidding farewell to the beloved
tree might be easier.

00:06:48.100 --> 00:06:50.660
Like, say, Peter Quill!

00:06:50.660 --> 00:06:52.569
Now that would be a better plan.

00:06:52.569 --> 00:06:54.919
"I like your plan, except, it sucks.

00:06:54.919 --> 00:06:57.949
So let me do the plan, and that way, it might
be really good."

00:06:59.139 --> 00:07:03.400
With two solo films and two team-ups under
his belt, Scott Lang has become a staple in

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:04.419
the MCU.

00:07:04.419 --> 00:07:08.139
Serving as one of the sillier characters in
the film universe, Scott instantly got the

00:07:08.139 --> 00:07:11.960
fandom behind him, and he's become one of
the MCU's leading stars with characters like

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:15.340
Tony Stark, Steve Rogers, and Natasha Romanoff
out of the game.

00:07:15.340 --> 00:07:20.100
If Scott were to die in the upcoming "Ant-Man
and the Wasp: Quantumania" or another team-up

00:07:20.100 --> 00:07:23.720
film, the MCU fandom would riot — on their
computers.

00:07:23.720 --> 00:07:28.220
It's not so much that killing off Ant-Man
would devastate moviegoers, as much as saying

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:30.409
goodbye to star Paul Rudd would.

00:07:30.409 --> 00:07:35.150
His comedy never feels forced, and there is
so much more to explore with the character.

00:07:35.150 --> 00:07:40.050
No more Scott means no more Rudd in Marvel
projects, and that's not something we're prepared

00:07:40.050 --> 00:07:41.840
to handle just yet.

00:07:42.840 --> 00:07:46.509
Wanda Maximoff has one of the most complex
story arcs in all of the MCU.

00:07:46.509 --> 00:07:50.159
As a matter of fact, it doesn't seem like
her arc is even close to being finished at

00:07:50.159 --> 00:07:55.199
this point as she has only recently become
the Scarlet Witch after the events of "WandaVision."

00:07:55.199 --> 00:08:00.129
While it looks like she might be on the path
to darkness, watching Wanda die would be pretty

00:08:00.129 --> 00:08:01.129
painful.

00:08:01.129 --> 00:08:05.620
We know the true, good-natured Wanda is still
in there somewhere — we're just hoping light

00:08:05.620 --> 00:08:08.189
triumphs over evil in her next few appearances.

00:08:08.189 --> 00:08:09.189
That's all.

00:08:09.189 --> 00:08:13.240
Wanda has had way too much happen to her in
her life, from the death of her parents, to

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:18.039
the death of her brother Pietro, to the many
deaths of Vision, to the complete breakdown

00:08:18.039 --> 00:08:22.389
of her not-so-happily-ever-after in Westview
— the woman needs a break.

00:08:22.389 --> 00:08:27.689
If anyone deserves a happy ending, it's Wanda,
and that certainly isn't going to happen with

00:08:27.689 --> 00:08:28.689
her death.

00:08:28.689 --> 00:08:29.860
"That doesn't seem fair!"

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:36.220
There are awesome MCU characters, and then
there are protect-at-all-costs characters,

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:38.969
and one of those is Mr. Jimmy Woo.

00:08:38.969 --> 00:08:43.550
First debuting in "Ant-Man and the Wasp,"
Jimmy was a funny, quirky FBI agent assigned

00:08:43.550 --> 00:08:45.470
as Scott Lang's parole officer.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:50.000
There is something so endearing about Jimmy,
which was further amplified when he showed

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:51.850
up in Westview for "WandaVision."

00:08:51.850 --> 00:08:55.560
He fights for the side of good and rebels
against leadership when he knows something

00:08:55.560 --> 00:08:56.620
is afoot.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:01.269
The allure of Jimmy Woo is similar to that
of his frenemy Scott Lang, as both characters

00:09:01.269 --> 00:09:03.480
are played by actors loved by the public.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:07.250
If anyone played Jimmy other than Randall
Park, fans across the globe might have been

00:09:07.250 --> 00:09:09.630
less likely to fall in love with the agent.

00:09:09.630 --> 00:09:13.860
Throughout the airing of "WandaVision," viewers
campaigned across social media to get Jimmy

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.050
his own spinoff series, according to The Direct.

00:09:17.050 --> 00:09:22.360
Some Redditors even dubbed him the best new
Marvel character, so if he dies off in a future

00:09:22.360 --> 00:09:26.160
phase, we can expect some serious backlash
from fans.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:32.080
One of the best moves ever made in the MCU's
casting history was the switch from Terrence

00:09:32.080 --> 00:09:35.519
Howard to Don Cheadle for the part of Colonel
James Rhodes.

00:09:35.519 --> 00:09:40.050
Sometimes those kinds of actor replacements
can ruin the movie, but that wasn't the case

00:09:40.050 --> 00:09:41.120
at all here.

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:45.180
Rhodes is another of Tony Stark's closest
friends and confidants who always has his

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.180
back.

00:09:46.180 --> 00:09:49.310
He's also instrumental in the fight against
Thanos and one of the few who participates

00:09:49.310 --> 00:09:50.460
in the Time Heist.

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:55.829
We've been through so much with Rhodes that
seeing him go down would be difficult to watch.

00:09:55.829 --> 00:09:59.490
Case in point, it looked like Rhodes met his
end in "Captain America: Civil War" after

00:09:59.490 --> 00:10:02.110
Vision accidentally knocked him out of the
sky.

00:10:02.110 --> 00:10:06.320
When he hit the ground, audiences across the
world gasped.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:10.890
It was a moment when many MCU fans realized
they cared a hell of a lot more about the

00:10:10.890 --> 00:10:12.160
character than they thought they did.

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:16.700
It would be tough to watch that kind of moment
again with Rhodes, as we need as many people

00:10:16.700 --> 00:10:19.300
as we can to carry on the memory of Iron Man.

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:24.149
With Cheadle set to return in the upcoming
Disney+ series "Armor Wars," we hope nothing

00:10:24.149 --> 00:10:27.260
but good things are on the horizon for War
Machine.

00:10:28.260 --> 00:10:32.089
We've seen a love interest of Spider-Man die
on the big screen before, and it's nothing

00:10:32.089 --> 00:10:33.970
we're interested in going through again.

00:10:33.970 --> 00:10:38.991
The death of Gwen Stacy in "The Amazing Spider-Man
2" was a total shock (except to anyone who

00:10:38.991 --> 00:10:43.190
has ever read the comics, of course), and
if that type of twist was delivered twice

00:10:43.190 --> 00:10:47.149
to Spider-Man fans, it would be way out of
bounds.

00:10:47.149 --> 00:10:51.740
Zendaya does an incredible job portraying
MJ in the MCU's "Spider-Man" films, and following

00:10:51.740 --> 00:10:55.925
the events of "Spider-Man: Far From Home,"
it would be even more devastating to lose her.

00:10:55.925 --> 00:11:00.390
Sometimes close friends and love interests
are killed off in films to give the protagonist

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:05.459
the push they need to defeat the big bad,
but we're hoping that's not a route the MCU

00:11:05.459 --> 00:11:06.500
takes with MJ.

00:11:06.500 --> 00:11:12.700
With a talent like Zendaya on your roster,
it's best to keep her around as long as possible.

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:19.079
It took all of one episode for "Loki" viewers
to fall in love with Mobius M. Mobius, the

00:11:19.079 --> 00:11:22.420
Time Variance Authority agent played by the
charming Owen Wilson.

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:27.670
The actor had undeniable chemistry with Loki
himself, Tom Hiddleston, and every scene involving

00:11:27.670 --> 00:11:29.940
the duo was pure magic.

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:34.970
Fans absolutely lost their minds when Mobius
seemingly died in Episode 4 of the series

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.070
after being pruned by Judge Renslayer.

00:11:37.070 --> 00:11:42.740
We had only known him for a few episodes,
but the determined yet kind TVA agent became

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:44.450
a favorite in no time.

00:11:44.450 --> 00:11:49.060
Thankfully, we found out in Episode 5 that
one doesn't die when they're pruned but instead

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.990
transported to The Void at the End of Time.

00:11:51.990 --> 00:11:57.060
It's usually a death sentence, but Mobius
was able to get out, in addition to surviving

00:11:57.060 --> 00:12:01.410
all the events of "Loki," which suggests we
will see Wilson back in action.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:06.290
If we lose Mobius in a future MCU project,
fans will not go quietly.

00:12:06.290 --> 00:12:10.570
For weeks, the fandom took to social media
to express their love for the mustache-rocking

00:12:10.570 --> 00:12:15.050
agent, with many a thread on Reddit dedicated
to the hopes of seeing Mobius on a jet ski

00:12:15.050 --> 00:12:16.310
in the future.

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:21.990
If he does die — which he better not — we
just hope he has one hell of a ride on a Sea-Doo

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.600
before biting the bullet.

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:28.740
Wong is a force to be reckoned with in the
MCU, and we're not quite sure the sorcerer's

00:12:28.740 --> 00:12:31.050
full potential has been revealed just yet.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:34.800
When he first debuted in "Doctor Strange,"
it seemed like Wong would primarily serve

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.490
as a sidekick to Stephen Strange, but the
last several years have proven he's his own

00:12:39.490 --> 00:12:40.490
man.

00:12:40.490 --> 00:12:44.980
Wong has shown up in five different MCU flicks
and also has a big role in "Doctor Strange

00:12:44.980 --> 00:12:46.690
in the Multiverse of Madness."

00:12:46.690 --> 00:12:51.490
If Wong is killed off, it's going to send
some serious waves through fandom.

00:12:51.490 --> 00:12:56.070
The character is undoubtedly a fan favorite
thanks to his dedication to his craft and

00:12:56.070 --> 00:12:57.589
perfectly timed one-liners.

00:12:57.589 --> 00:13:04.870
"It's funny!"

00:13:04.870 --> 00:13:10.820
Wong feels like a security blanket, always
there to protect you and make you feel warm

00:13:10.820 --> 00:13:12.110
and fuzzy.

00:13:12.110 --> 00:13:16.700
Losing Wong wouldn't just be a blow to the
fans, but the MCU as a whole — especially

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:18.120
Doctor Strange.

00:13:18.120 --> 00:13:22.250
Without Wong to keep the Sorcerer Supreme
in line, the ramifications of losing him could

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:25.100
be catastrophic to the entire MCU.

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:30.050
Shuri just might be the most intelligent character
in the MCU right now.

00:13:30.050 --> 00:13:33.890
Rocket might give her a run for her money,
but with Tony Stark in the ground and the

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:38.029
Hulk constantly switching between forms, the
Wakandan is one of the brightest minds on

00:13:38.029 --> 00:13:39.029
the planet.

00:13:39.029 --> 00:13:42.899
While it's still up in the air what role she
will move into in "Black Panther: Wakanda

00:13:42.899 --> 00:13:46.820
Forever," Shuri is likely to play a more significant
role in the MCU as a whole.

00:13:46.820 --> 00:13:51.100
The loss of Shuri isn't something audiences
would handle very well, especially since she

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.779
is the only child of King T'Chaka left.

00:13:53.779 --> 00:13:58.410
And as with Okoye, it would be pretty difficult
to see the loss of another major Wakandan

00:13:58.410 --> 00:13:59.410
character.

00:13:59.410 --> 00:14:03.899
Shuri has so much to offer the world and her
superhero friends that her loss would be devastating

00:14:03.899 --> 00:14:06.149
on so many levels.

00:14:06.149 --> 00:14:10.220
Justifying her death would be a difficult
task for writers, and we're hoping she sticks

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:11.780
around for quite some time.

00:14:12.780 --> 00:14:15.550
Talk about an MCU character who has been through
the wringer.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:20.720
Bucky Barnes — aka the Winter Soldier — has
appeared in five films and one Disney+ series,

00:14:20.720 --> 00:14:23.209
serving as the loyal best friend of Steve
Rogers.

00:14:23.209 --> 00:14:27.351
Despite his hardened exterior, Bucky has long
been a fan-favorite in the MCU who has one

00:14:27.351 --> 00:14:30.490
of the most tragic character arcs in the Infinity
Saga.

00:14:30.490 --> 00:14:36.060
He has persevered despite being brainwashed
by the enemy, and comes full circle and repents

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.509
for his past transgressions in "The Falcon
and the Winter Soldier."

00:14:39.509 --> 00:14:43.110
Some fans on Reddit were bummed out that he
didn't take on the mantle of Captain America

00:14:43.110 --> 00:14:47.290
as Steve Rogers passed over his shield, but
Bucky himself seemed to agree the honor belonged

00:14:47.290 --> 00:14:48.410
to Sam Wilson.

00:14:48.410 --> 00:14:53.160
Bucky has an all-around good heart, and fans
have only ever wanted the best for him, given

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:54.890
his tragic past with Hydra.

00:14:54.890 --> 00:14:59.630
If he were to die in an upcoming project after
the beautiful closure he had in "The Falcon

00:14:59.630 --> 00:15:02.500
and the Winter Soldier," it would be a travesty.

00:15:02.500 --> 00:15:07.790
Some people just deserve goodness thrown their
way, and Bucky is one of them.

00:15:08.790 --> 00:15:12.950
"Hawkeye" turned out to be one incredible
ride and introduced one of the most fun and

00:15:12.950 --> 00:15:15.640
exciting MCU characters of the last few years.

00:15:15.640 --> 00:15:20.250
Hailee Steinfeld absolutely nailed the role
of Kate Bishop — a stellar archer who was

00:15:20.250 --> 00:15:25.500
inspired by Clint Barton when she saw him
defending New York from the Chitauri in 2012.

00:15:25.500 --> 00:15:30.730
Her constant fangirling over Clint was perfectly
ironic, given how there has always been a

00:15:30.730 --> 00:15:35.020
debate amongst MCU fans whether Hawkeye might
be the worst Avenger.

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:39.339
Kate is a wonderfully naive character who
is still learning who she is and what her

00:15:39.339 --> 00:15:41.389
place is in this superhero world.

00:15:41.389 --> 00:15:45.920
This type of young hero is exactly what the
MCU needs moving forward, and taking her out

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:48.730
too soon would be a big hit for the fan base.

00:15:48.730 --> 00:15:53.329
There is also much to discover between Kate
and Yelena Belova, and fans are certainly

00:15:53.329 --> 00:15:56.759
shipping that potential friendship, whose
roots were laid in "Hawkeye."

00:15:56.759 --> 00:16:02.699
These two have the potential to be the MCU's
next besties, so they must be protected 

00:16:02.699 --> 00:16:03.899
at all costs.

